  "id": "DrugBank_DB01200 - MONDO_10709",
  "verbalization": "Bromocriptine is linked to Early-onset Parkinsonism-intellectual Disability Syndrome through a series of indications that suggest a potential pathophysiological mechanism. The evidence indicates that Bromocriptine is associated with Juvenile Onset Parkinson Disease 19a and Parkinson Disease, both of which are indicated to interact with Cycrimine and Istradefylline, respectively. These intermediaries are further linked to the target syndrome, suggesting a possible pathway where Bromocriptine may influence the development of Parkinson disease through interactions with these compounds. The overlapping indications and the shared outcome imply a potential role for Bromocriptine in the pathogenesis of this syndrome, possibly through mechanisms involving dopamine modulation or other neurochemical pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of considering the broader pharmacological context in assessing the reusability of Bromocriptine for this condition.",
